# LeakSanitizer suppressions: leaks in system libraries we can't fix.
#
# Keep this list short and specific. Every entry hides real reports, so only
# add a library after checking that the leaked memory is allocated inside it
# (the first frames of the report), not in Palang's code.

# fontconfig caches font configuration and match results for the lifetime of
# the process and never frees them at exit.
leak:libfontconfig.so

# GTK's IBus input-method module leaks IBusText objects while handling focus
# and key events (found in Phase 0 manual test 3).
leak:libim-ibus.so

# GtkSourceView's file loader leaks one small block (about the size of the
# text) when it converts a non-UTF-8 file (e.g. Latin-1) to UTF-8. It's
# allocated by its internal buffer output stream, inside g_output_stream_write.
# Matching that frame (not all of libgtksourceview) keeps leaks caused by our
# own use of GtkSourceView objects visible. Found by
# tests/test-document.c (save-keeps-encoding).
leak:g_output_stream_write
